## Pattern 8: Form Design (Minimal Data Entry)

**Use Case:** Design forms that minimize user input

```xml
<!-- views/fms_shift_form.xml -->
<form string="Shift">
    <header>
        <button name="action_open_shift" string="Open Shift" type="object" />
        <button name="action_close_shift" string="Close Shift" type="object" />
        <field name="status" widget="statusbar" />
    </header>
    
    <sheet>
        <!-- COLLAPSIBLE SECTION: Header (always visible) -->
        <group>
            <field name="name" readonly="1" />
            <field name="shift_date" />
            <field name="supervisor_id" />
        </group>
        
        <!-- COLLAPSIBLE SECTION: Dips (editable) -->
        <separator string="Tank Dips" />
        <field name="dip_entry_line_ids">
            <tree editable="bottom">
                <field name="tank_id" readonly="1" />
                <field name="opening_vol" readonly="1" />
                <field name="closing_vol" required="1" />
                <field name="variance_pct" readonly="1" />
            </tree>
        </field>
        
        <!-- COLLAPSIBLE SECTION: Meters (editable) -->
        <separator string="Pump Meters" />
        <field name="meter_entry_line_ids">
            <tree editable="bottom">
                <field name="pump_id" readonly="1" />
                <field name="nozzle_id" readonly="1" />
                <field name="opening_elec_vol" readonly="1" />
                <field name="closing_elec_vol" required="1" />
                <field name="qty_sold" readonly="1" />
            </tree>
        </field>
        
        <!-- COLLAPSIBLE SECTION: Reconciliation (read-only) -->
        <separator string="Reconciliation Results" />
        <group>
            <field name="fc_cash_balance" readonly="1" />
            <field name="total_attendant_variance" readonly="1" />
        </group>
    </sheet>
</form>
```

**Key Points:**
- Use `readonly="1"` for auto-populated fields (opening readings)
- Use `required="1"` for mandatory user entry (closing readings)
- Use `editable="bottom"` for inline editing in lists
- Use separators for sections (not headers)
- Minimize scrolling (fit on one screen if possible)
- Use status bar for state machine

---

## Best Practices Summary

1. **Immutability:** Make logs immutable (prevent post-close edits)
2. **Hard Gates:** No overrides, no "close anyway" buttons
3. **Audit Trail:** Store all changes (Odoo's tracking module)
4. **No Parallel Bookkeeping:** All data posts to GL
5. **Minimal Entry:** Auto-fetch opening readings, compute everything else
6. **Single Form:** One shift form, not multiple models/menus
7. **GL Integration:** Use Odoo core (don't reinvent accounting)
8. **Testing:** 80%+ coverage, test hard gates explicitly
9. **Performance:** Avoid N+1 queries (use ORM grouping)
10. **Compliance:** Immutable logs meet regulatory audit requirements

